.TH GIT-OPEN 1 "2026-11-16" "git-open" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-open \- open a git repository, file, or commit in the browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git-open
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ path | commit ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-open
opens the web page of the current repository's remote, at the current branch. With
an argument, it opens that file, folder, line, or commit instead.
.PP
Hosts build URLs differently, so
.B git-open
picks a provider, the URL rules for one host, from the remote URL. Built in are
github.com, gitlab.com, bitbucket.org, and codeberg.org. To add another, see
.BR CONFIGURATION .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-ref " " \fIref\fR
Open at a branch, tag, or commit instead of the current branch. Applies to the
repository root, files, and folders. It cannot be combined with a
.I commit
argument. The ref is used literally and is not checked, so origin/main 404s. The
.BI \-\-ref= ref
form is also accepted.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-remote " " \fIname\fR
Build the URL from the named remote instead of the default remote. The
.BI \-\-remote= name
form is also accepted. An unknown remote is an error. Combines with
.BR \-\-ref .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-browser
Print the URL to standard output instead of opening it in the browser.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit. Git intercepts
.B git open \-\-help
to show this page, so use
.B \-h
for the usage text.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
Treat every following argument as a path, even if it begins with a dash.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I path
A file or folder in the repository. A trailing
.I :line
or
.I :start\-end
opens that line or range of lines of a file. The suffix is ignored for a folder.
A path outside the repository, or \fB\&.\fR at its root, opens the tree URL at
the ref.
.TP
.I commit
A commit hash of 7 to 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 on success, including \fB\-h\fR and \fB\-v\fR. Any error exits 1 and
prints a line beginning
.B error:
to standard error.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Providers other than github.com, gitlab.com, bitbucket.org and codeberg.org
are added with git config. Local repository config takes precedence over global.
The
.I url
must be an http or https URL with a host. A provider missing a required key is
skipped.
.TP
.B open.<url>.commitprefix
Path segment between the repository and a commit hash. Required.
.TP
.B open.<url>.pathprefix
Path segment between the repository and a ref. Required.
.TP
.B open.<url>.lineformat
Line anchor template where
.B %l
is a line number. At most two
.B %l
may be given, for the start and end lines. Optional. If it is missing or
invalid, only line anchors are dropped, and a warning is printed to standard
error.
.PP
.RS
.EX
git config \-\-global open.https://git.example.com.commitprefix commit
git config \-\-global open.https://git.example.com.pathprefix tree
git config \-\-global open.https://git.example.com.lineformat "L%l\-L%l"
.EE
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
$ git open
$ git open main.go
$ git open main.go:42\-50
$ git open 7605d91
$ git open main.go \-n
$ git open main.go \-\-ref v1.0.0
$ git open main.go \-R fork
$ git \-C ~/src/my\-repo open
$ git open \-\- \-odd\-file\-name
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1)
